A||||3||WayneF||86 to 88 engine cradle swap||||1
Z||000000||WayneF||10-11-1999||03:30 PM||||I recently bought a Countach replica based on an 88 fiero with a 4spd, 4cyl.  Not wanting the sound or performance of the 4cyl, I just bought an 85 GT frame with 6 cyl, 4spd.  My plan is to do the entire engine cradle swap with struts so I can still drive it, then build up a 3800 or V8 on the 88 cradle.  I know the cradles are built different, but do they mount the same or what problems will there be?  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||10-11-1999||03:46 PM||||A few things, mainly the complete crade and suspension needs to be switched over.<P>The biggest issue is the the strut mounts at the top are in a different position. Ryane makes a kit to adapt the 86 towers to the 88 strut positions. I know someone that has done the swap. If you like I can have them email you.<P>It didn't sound too bad if you have a donor vehicle.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||WayneF||10-11-1999||05:05 PM||||Thanks, I would like any info on what the adapters look like, I have access to a full machine shop, making an adapter that I could later remove when putting in the 88 cradle would be desirable.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mwbackus||10-11-1999||07:40 PM||||Try here:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.ryanemotorsports.com/88cradle.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ryanemotorsports.com/88cradle.htm</A> <P>Mike||||reg||1
